// The `type` package is the auto-imported core bundle that backs the native
// numeric types. It has no callable API: programs use the numeric types
// (`u8`…`i64`, `f32`, `f64`, `boolean`) as native language types without
// importing them.
//
// Under the hood it generates `core_type.h`, which provides the C++ aliases
// (`using u8 = uint8_t`, etc.) and the `nullable<T>` wrapper that the codegen
// relies on when emitting C++. It also acts as the bundle root for the runtime
// sub-libraries `array`, `string` and `int128`, whose headers are generated
// into the same build directory and pulled in from `core_type.h`.
